      "caveat": "Cumulative incidence of the first brain metastasis after the study's day 0, with death (OS_STATUS) as a competing risk: Aalen–Johansen, 95% intervals from its delta-method standard error. It is not 1 − Kaplan–Meier: that treats the dead as still at risk of the event and overstates incidence whenever death is common — the table sets the two side by side. Excluded rather than counted as event-free: 2101 who already had it by day 0, 0 without follow-up. Gray's test (weight 1) by permutation of cohort labels, 2000 shuffles, seeded; exact under the null that the cohorts share one distribution, entry times included. An event recorded from notes or registries is only as complete as the recording.",
